NV_PK(24,{"a hsia in tainan is famous for this dish its rice is long grain sticky rice mixed with mushrooms dried shrimp minced pork dried scallops and fried shallots and fat crabs full of roe cover the top ming fu in taipei is a small restaurant with only a few tables the owner's cooking earned it a michelin star red crab sticky rice and buddha jumps over the wall are its famous dishes and you must book ahead":"","wa gui shops usually sell thick fish soup too made with small pieces of fish paste one wa gui and one bowl of fish soup is a brunch every tainan local knows fu sheng hao near chihkan tower and yi wei pin on guohua street are two famous old wa gui shops":"","mi gao is a snack made from sticky rice but it looks different in different parts of taiwan in tainan it is a small bowl of steamed white sticky rice with a spoonful of braised minced pork on top plus fish floss cucumber slices and a few braised peanuts":"","the key to good tainan mi gao is the rice the sticky rice is soaked and then steamed and each grain should be separate and springy not mushy some old shops still keep the rice warm in a wooden or straw tub":""});